<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="robots" content="noindex,nofollow"><title>Chinese 4 · Paper A · Learner paper</title><base href="/api/v1/course-tests/chinese-4/a/file/"><link rel="stylesheet" href="paper.css"></head><body><main><header class="hero"><p class="eyebrow">HSKKit · Chinese 4 Course Review · Original Paper A</p><h1>Learner paper</h1><p>40 objective questions + 4 writing/speaking tasks · 100-minute section budget.</p><p class="note">Reference materials. Open the workspace for section clocks, local answer saving and recording. Writing and speaking need self-review or your own teacher; no automatic grade.</p><nav class="links"><a href="index.html">Overview</a><a href="student.html">Learner paper</a><a href="student-traditional.html">繁體試卷</a><a href="teacher.html">Answers &amp; scripts</a><a href="listening.html">Listen to Chinese 4 A</a><a href="student.pdf">Learner PDF</a><a href="student-traditional.pdf">繁體 PDF</a><a href="teacher.pdf">Answer PDF</a></nav></header><nav class="links"><a href="#listening">Listening</a><a href="#reading">Reading</a><a href="#writing">Writing</a><a href="#speaking">Speaking</a></nav><h2 class="section-title" id="listening">Listening · 30 minutes</h2><h3>L1 · Questions 1–5</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/listening-group-1.mp3"></audio><p class="note">7:30 group track: 1 + 2 + 2 questions across three sources; each source plays twice, with answering pauses.</p><section class="material-block" data-material="C4A-L1a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 1</p><p class="gloss">标题: title</p><p class="gloss">保留: retain</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q1"><h3>1. What does the speaker explicitly want to retain?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 只有英文的说明</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 去年的全部展品</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 原来的中文名字</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C4A-L1b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 2, 3 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">背景: background</p><p class="gloss">规定: rule</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q2"><h3>2. What experience will the man describe?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 妹妹在外地参加比赛</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 全家刚制定的新规定</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 小时候与爷爷准备晚饭</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q3"><h3>3. Why will the two recordings be presented together?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 展示不同背景下做法的变化</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 证明妹妹必须恢复旧做法</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 选出唯一正确的做菜顺序</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C4A-L1c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 4, 5 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">值班: be on duty</p><p class="gloss">成品: finished work</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q4"><h3>4. What was the organizer’s stated purpose?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 让新伙伴轻松认识彼此</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 要求伙伴提前交翻译成品</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 当场选出最好的演讲者</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q5"><h3>5. What most likely caused the misunderstanding?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 伙伴认为自己的翻译已经被拒绝</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 双方把非正式见面理解成不同的参与要求</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 组织者临时把会议改成了值班</div></div></article></div></section><h3>L2 · Questions 6–10</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/listening-group-2.mp3"></audio><p class="note">7:30 group track: 1 + 2 + 2 questions across three sources; each source plays twice, with answering pauses.</p><section class="material-block" data-material="C4A-L2a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 6</p><p class="gloss">设备测试: device check</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q6"><h3>6. What must participants prepare?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 看照片后提出一个相关问题</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 交一篇完整的文化研究报告</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 周三完成正式交流</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C4A-L2b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 7, 8 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">并排: side by side</p><p class="gloss">译文: translation</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q7"><h3>7. What useful function do both users describe?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 保证所有称呼和地名都准确</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 完全代替讲故事的人审核</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 帮助更快地完成初步语言处理</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q8"><h3>8. Which improvement best addresses both reports?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 原文译文并排，修改留标记，确认后发布</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 隐藏原文，自动发布全部译文</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 只提高发布速度，不保留修改记录</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C4A-L2c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 9, 10 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">预约: reserve</p><p class="gloss">试行: trial implementation</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q9"><h3>9. Which rule is explicitly proposed for every group?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 不用预约的组可以一直使用</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 每组最多使用三十分钟</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 靠窗区域改为自由讨论区</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q10"><h3>10. Why does the man accept the trial conditionally?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 已经证明新规则对所有人都最好</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 希望取消全部需要预约的时段</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 兼顾临时需要，并用时限和记录检查影响</div></div></article></div></section><h3>L3 · Questions 11–15</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/listening-group-3.mp3"></audio><p class="note">7:30 group track: 1 + 2 + 2 questions across three sources; each source plays twice, with answering pauses.</p><section class="material-block" data-material="C4A-L3a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 11</p><p class="gloss">导演: director</p><p class="gloss">放映: screening</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q11"><h3>11. What is the main purpose of the screening?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 讨论细节如何支持不同理解</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 教授照片分类的唯一方法</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 让观众背出统一的感想</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C4A-L3b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 12, 13 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">旁白: voice-over</p><p class="gloss">停顿: pause</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q12"><h3>12. How does the pause help communicate the character’s feelings?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 表明他已经决定不参加活动</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 与不敢开口的前话相连，表现犹豫</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 说明他一定在门外等朋友</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q13"><h3>13. Which view best represents the filmmaker’s attitude?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 允许不同理解，但需要画面依据</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 只接受导演本人说出的唯一答案</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 所有与画面无关的猜想都同样合理</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C4A-L3c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 14, 15 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">归还: return borrowed items</p><p class="gloss">储存架: storage rack</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q14"><h3>14. What resource does Plan A explicitly have?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 周末全天开放的清洗室</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 周五可用的清洗室和两位清洗者</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 足够所有活动同时使用的杯子</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q15"><h3>15. Which action is best supported by both proposals?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 只要杯子有一百个就立即全面推广</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 先按甲试一次，推广前补足清洗存放安排</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 先取消周五清洗，再增加周末活动</div></div></article></div></section><h3>L4 · Questions 16–20</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/listening-group-4.mp3"></audio><p class="note">7:30 group track: 1 + 2 + 2 questions across three sources; each source plays twice, with answering pauses.</p><section class="material-block" data-material="C4A-L4a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 16</p><p class="gloss">破损: damaged</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q16"><h3>16. What condition remains unchanged?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 每个人仍须自己排队送杯子</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 破损杯一律记成未归还</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 仍须在周五下午清洗</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C4A-L4b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 17, 18 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">识别: recognize</p><p class="gloss">导览: navigation guide</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q17"><h3>17. What helps explain the different trial results?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 工具在所有地点都从未出现错误</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 新同学都拒绝接受操作说明</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 标记亮度和使用者操作经验不同</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q18"><h3>18. Which conclusion goes beyond the interview evidence?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 部分使用者学习操作后能找到地点</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 所有新生在任何地点都不再需要帮助</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 改善较暗地点的标记值得继续试验</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C4A-L4c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 19, 20 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">勾选: tick an option</p><p class="gloss">个体: individual</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q19"><h3>19. How did the organizers respond to the objections?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 取消所有共同结构，只留下工作人员评论</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 保留简表，同时加入经本人核对的故事录音</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 要求每个家庭都承认做法从未改变</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q20"><h3>20. How has the speaker’s understanding of tradition developed?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 开始重视讲述者、改变原因和仍保留的意义</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 认为只要有变化就不再有任何传统意义</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 认为所有家庭最终都应该采用同一种做法</div></div></article></div></section><h2 class="section-title" id="reading">Reading · 30 minutes</h2><h3>R1 · Questions 21–25</h3><section class="material-block" data-material="C4A-R1a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 21</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">这次社区故事展给每段录音设计了新的英文标题，方便不同语言的邻居寻找内容。策划人仍把讲述者选定的中文名字印在旁边，字号和英文一样大。志愿者建议把不容易翻译的名字删掉，讲述者却认为，名字与自己的经历相连，不能只因翻译麻烦就取消。最后双方决定保留中文，并用一句简短英文解释名字的来由。解释须先交本人确认，才印成展签。</p></div><p class="gloss">展签: exhibit label</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q21"><h3>21. Which element will definitely be retained on the label?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 讲述者选定的中文名字</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 志愿者写的全部翻译意见</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 只有英文而没有中文的标题</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C4A-R1b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 22, 23 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">小时候，小岚每年都与外婆一起写手工菜单，把当天要做的饭菜记下来。她记得最清楚的不是菜的数量，而是外婆讲述每个菜名时的语气。因此，她准备在故事展里放一张旧菜单，并配上自己的回忆录音。她在介绍里写明，这只是自己与外婆的经验，不能代表所有家庭。<br>弟弟现在在外地学习，平时用手机与家人商量吃什么。他提议再放一张聊天记录的模拟图，说明今天的联系方法。小岚起初觉得新图会破坏旧菜单的意义，听完弟弟的解释后，同意把两者并列。她发现，保留共同商量饭菜的习惯，不一定要求每次都使用同一种工具。展示只用重新编写的例子，不公开家人的真实聊天内容。</p></div><p class="gloss">并列: display alongside</p><p class="gloss">模拟图: illustrative mock-up</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q22"><h3>22. What does Xiaolan explicitly say her recording represents?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 她与外婆的一段个人经验</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 所有家庭都必须遵守的做法</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 弟弟完整真实的聊天内容</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q23"><h3>23. Why does she eventually accept the new illustration?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 旧菜单已经完全失去家庭意义</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 工具改变仍可延续共同商量的习惯</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 手机工具能证明所有旧习惯都应取消</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C4A-R1c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 24, 25 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">材料甲，交流邀请：周二午休请两校代表先到线上房间碰面。此次只是认识伙伴、确认后续分工，不需要准备正式展示。每位代表仍需到场，若时间有困难，请提前留言。文化故事的翻译工作在下次会议才开始。请不要为了这次碰面赶写成品。<br>材料乙，伙伴回复：我看到“不需要正式展示”，以为午休那次可以不去，就报名参加了同一时间的排练。读到老师转来的补充说明，才发现每位代表都应该参加。我想调整排练时间，并询问是否可以提前十分钟结束。如果不能，我会先说明冲突，请大家确认可否由另一位代表代替，不能直接当作已经请好假。</p></div><p class="gloss">代表: representative</p><p class="gloss">排练: rehearsal</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q24"><h3>24. What does the invitation explicitly require?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 代表先交完整翻译作品</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 代表到场认识伙伴并确认分工</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 所有代表必须在碰面时演讲</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q25"><h3>25. Which clarification would best resolve the stated misunderstanding?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 区分不必展示和仍需到场，另确认时间冲突</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 说明翻译已经通过验收，无须再来</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 要求伙伴删除全部排练安排</div></div></article></div></section><h3>R2 · Questions 26–30</h3><section class="material-block" data-material="C4A-R2a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 26</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">两校下周举行线上交流，每位参加者须先读一张伙伴提供的生活照片卡，记下一个想进一步了解的问题。照片旁已经解释可能陌生的词，因此不要求学生另外搜索文化知识。主持人提醒，问题要围绕卡片中的具体细节，不能请一位伙伴代表整个国家。若照片中的人物不愿回答私人经历，可以只讨论图片里已经给出的信息。活动后每人整理一条得到澄清的认识。</p></div><p class="gloss">主持人: host</p><p class="gloss">澄清: clarify</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q26"><h3>26. What preparation does the notice require?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 查询并背熟全部文化背景</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 读照片卡并准备一个相关问题</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 要求伙伴披露真实私人经历</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C4A-R2b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 27, 28 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">材料甲，试用记录：展览翻译工具让六段中文简介很快有了英文初稿。检查时发现，普通物品名称大多清楚，但同一个人的称呼前后不同。试用组建议保留原文和译文，先由熟悉内容的人确认，再公开。记录只涉及这六段文字，没有测试口头对话或其他题材。<br>材料乙，接待组回复：我们愿意继续试用，不过需要知道每次修改了哪里。上次有人改正一个名字，另一位同学却拿旧版本去印，造成两套展签。请在并排页面上标出改动，并让确认后的版本有清楚日期。对接待组来说，速度有帮助，但能找到最新且核对过的文字更重要。现阶段不能把“很快有初稿”写成“所有内容都已准确翻译”。</p></div><p class="gloss">版本: version</p><p class="gloss">初稿: first draft</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q27"><h3>27. What is the tool’s demonstrated useful role?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 保证所有题材与口头对话都准确</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 让接待组完全不必再核对名字</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 快速提供供人工核对的英文初稿</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q28"><h3>28. Which revision addresses both documents?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 原译文并排，标改动与日期，确认后再印</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 删除原文，把所有初稿立即自动印出</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 只统一页面颜色，不显示修改或日期</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C4A-R2c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 29, 30 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">图书馆原来把讨论室全部改成预约使用，有同学反映，临时遇到小组问题时常常找不到当天的空位。管理组提出两周试行办法：周一与周四午休各留一个房间，不预约也可排队使用，但每组最多二十分钟；其他房间继续按预约安排。靠窗阅读区仍保持安静。<br>一位同学在意见栏中支持先试行，条件是把排队和超时情况记下来。他指出，留出临时时段也许能帮助部分人，但如果少数组一直超时，后面的人仍然没有机会。两周后应同时查看预约组与临时组的记录，再讨论是否调整房间数量。意见栏中的支持不表示他认为所有房间都该取消预约。</p></div><p class="gloss">超时: exceed the time limit</p><p class="gloss">意见栏: feedback section</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q29"><h3>29. What explicit exception does the trial introduce?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 所有房间永远不再接受预约</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 靠窗阅读区可以自由大声讨论</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 两天午休各有一间可排队使用的房间</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q30"><h3>30. Under what condition is the supporting student’s view best understood?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 有使用时限并依据两类记录评估试行</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 已经证明临时使用在所有情况下更公平</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 只记录预约者，不需要了解临时使用者</div></div></article></div></section><h3>R3 · Questions 31–35</h3><section class="material-block" data-material="C4A-R3a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 31</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">校园短片周的介绍说，作品《门口》用同一段进门前的画面，引出三位虚构同学不同的回忆。放映后的讨论面向普通观众，不要求知道电影术语。组织者请大家先说看见的动作、听见的话，再解释自己怎样理解人物。介绍没有给出标准感想，也不要求观众同意创作者的每个判断。如果观点不同，大家可以回到共同看到的细节继续讨论，而不是以谁更懂电影决定谁能发言。</p></div><p class="gloss">术语: technical terminology</p><p class="gloss">创作者: creator</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q31"><h3>31. Who is the discussion designed for, and what should they do?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 电影专家背诵统一术语和感想</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 普通观众根据共同细节解释人物</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 只有同意创作者的人才能发言</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C4A-R3b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 32, 33 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">原创微型故事：阿宁录好给旧朋友的问候，手指停在发送键上，却迟迟没有按下。去年两人因为一次误会很少联系。他删掉开头那句“你一定早就忘了”，换成“我还记得我们一起做展板的下午”。消息发出后，他把手机放进书包，走去参加社团活动。故事没有写朋友是否回复。<br>读书会的一段短评认为，删掉那句指责并不是阿宁不在乎过去，而是他试着从双方共有的经历重新开口。评论特别提到，最后把手机收起的动作，可以支持他愿意迈出一步、又不把当天全部心情交给等待的理解。不过这不足以证明两人已经和好，更不能替故事补出朋友的真实想法。其他读者可提出不同解释，但要说明依据在哪里。</p></div><p class="gloss">指责: blame</p><p class="gloss">短评: short commentary</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q32"><h3>32. Which change supports the commentary’s view of a new opening?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 删除全部问候且拒绝发送消息</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 收到朋友道歉以后才参加活动</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 把猜测朋友态度的话改为共同经历</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q33"><h3>33. Which inference is supported while respecting the story’s limit?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 朋友已经明确原谅并马上回复</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 把手机收起证明他再也不想联系</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 阿宁尝试联系，但尚不能确认双方已经和好</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C4A-R3c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 34, 35 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">材料甲，活动方案：环保组计划在周五的读书交流会借出八十个可重复使用的杯子。茶水台旁有清楚的归还箱，两位志愿者愿意收齐并在当天清洗。方案建议先记录借出、归还与损坏情况，活动后再决定是否给其他小组使用。暂不购买更多杯子。<br>材料乙，场地补充：周五清洗间可以用到下午五点，周末关闭；归还箱只能当日放在茶水台旁，不能长期占通道。已有小组想把杯子借到星期六，但还没有清洗地点和收回时间。负责人建议先完成周五试用，核对损坏和归还记录，再商量跨日借用的具体安排。参加者若带自己的杯子，也不影响本次记录，只须分开统计。</p></div><p class="gloss">跨日: across different days</p><p class="gloss">通道: passageway</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q34"><h3>34. Which resources are explicitly secured for Friday?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 周末清洗地点与长期通道储存位置</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 归还箱、两位志愿者及当天清洗条件</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 立即购买的新杯子和周六收杯人员</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q35"><h3>35. Which modification is supported by both texts?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 立即借到周六，不必再明确归还时间</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 把箱子永久放在通道，取消记录</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 先完成周五试用，跨日借用另定回收清洗</div></div></article></div></section><h3>R4 · Questions 36–40</h3><section class="material-block" data-material="C4A-R4a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 36</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">环保组把试用通知修改为：本周只在周五读书交流会使用共用杯，不接受周末跨日借用。各组可以由代表统一归还，但杯子要在下午四点半前送到茶水台旁；之后志愿者清洗。破损杯另放一箱，数量也要记录。带自用杯的人不用借杯，不计入未归还人数。本次结束后再按记录评估是否扩大，不能把一次活动的结果说成全校长期使用的效果。</p></div><p class="gloss">评估: evaluate</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q36"><h3>36. Which limit is explicitly stated?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 本周试用只限周五活动，不跨日借用</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 所有学生以后都不得带自用杯</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 一次记录已经代表全校长期效果</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C4A-R4b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 37, 38 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">材料甲，校园导览工具说明：工具读取教室旁的标记，显示从当前位置到目的地的路线。试用范围包括教学楼一层和二层。识别需要标记清楚、光线足够；说明没有承诺在标记损坏或光线不足时仍然准确。工具可以帮助找路，但不代替工作人员处理临时封闭区域。<br>材料乙，使用者反馈：我在一层主走廊三次顺利找到教室，在楼梯口遇到反光标记时却读错了。我请工作人员确认后，才知道该走另一边。另一位同学不熟悉拍摄操作，第一次也没成功，学习后才能使用。我支持修好标记后再扩大试用，但现有经历只覆盖少量地点和使用者，不能据此声称所有新生都可以完全独立地在全校通行。</p></div><p class="gloss">反光: reflective glare</p><p class="gloss">封闭: closed off</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q37"><h3>37. What explains why some attempts succeed while others do not?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 只要工具上线就不会读错任何标记</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 所有临时封闭区域都可由工具自动处理</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 标记条件和操作经验会影响识别使用</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q38"><h3>38. Which claim cannot be justified from these two sources?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 反光标记可能需要改善后再测试</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 部分人学习操作以后能够使用工具</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 所有新生已经可以在全校完全独立通行</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C4A-R4c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 39, 40 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">社区故事展起初规定，每位参与者只能填写同样的五个问题，工作人员再把答案做成统一图卡。一位参与者说，这样容易比较，却没有地方说明自己为什么改变做法。另一位参与者担心，若只展示一句话，观众会以为整个家庭都持相同看法。组织者于是保留图卡，同时增加可选的短录音，并把每张卡的讲述者写清楚。<br>录音整理后都交本人核对，愿意只填卡的人也可以不录音。试用结束时，工作人员发现，观众开始问“这位讲述者为什么这样选择”，而不只问“你们是不是都这样”。策划人在总结中说，统一格式有助于寻找信息，但认识文化还要听具体人物的理由。传统可以有延续，也可以有变化；仅凭一个故事，不足以推断每个家庭或每个地区的生活方式。</p></div><p class="gloss">持相同看法: share the same view</p><p class="gloss">格式: format</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q39"><h3>39. How did the organizers address different needs?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 取消图卡且强迫每个人提交私人录音</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 保留图卡，补充可选录音并标明讲述者</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 由工作人员替全部家庭决定唯一观点</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q40"><h3>40. Which conclusion best combines the experience and the reflection?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 只要统一格式就能概括所有地区的生活</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 格式帮助查找，理解文化还需联系具体人物理由</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 凡是改变形式的做法都失去文化意义</div></div></article></div></section><h2 class="section-title" id="writing">Writing · 30 minutes</h2><p>W1 and W2 share 30 minutes. Use paper or your own editor; this review page does not save answers.</p><section class="box" id="W1"><p class="eyebrow">writing · W1</p><h2>Reply to an exhibition disagreement</h2><p>Reply in Chinese to Mei. Answer whether you can join Friday lunchtime and whether you prefer printed cards or audio. Explain your choice, address the new restriction with a feasible adjustment, and ask a relevant confirmation. Invented details are fine. About 80–120 Chinese characters is guidance, not a minimum.</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">小安：故事展周五午休要最后检查，你能来吗？你觉得用印好的图卡，还是让大家听录音更合适？现在场地说不能外放声音，也不能把队伍排到走廊。我们原来想让全班同时听的办法行不通了。请说说你的选择和调整办法，也告诉我还有什么需要确认。小美</p></div><ul class="checklist"><li>Answer whether you can join Friday lunchtime.</li><li>Choose a suitable format.</li><li>State a clear position.</li><li>Give an audience-related reason.</li><li>Adjust for no loudspeaker and no corridor queue.</li><li>Ask a relevant confirmation.</li></ul><p class="badge">Manual /8 · no automatic grade</p></section><section class="box" id="W2"><p class="eyebrow">writing · W2</p><h2>Recommend an information display</h2><p>Write Chinese paragraphs for the student committee. Use at least one accurately attributed detail from EACH supplied source. Compare a benefit and a limitation, give your own conditional recommendation, and propose a practical next step. No outside research is needed. About 180–240 Chinese characters is guidance.</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">材料甲，图卡方案：把常用活动信息印在公告板旁，读者不用手机就能查看，初次制作费用四十元。若时间地点改变，需要重新印相应图卡。负责同学周一和周四可以检查更新，其他日子只能临时贴手写说明。<br>材料乙，电子页面方案：把信息集中在一个页面，可及时修改，不花印刷费。读者需要能上网的设备；校内有些访客没有手机。两位同学愿意维护页面，但还没有安排缺席时谁接替。委员会希望不同使用者都能找到可靠信息，现有预算五十元。</p></div><ul class="checklist"><li>Define the information-access problem.</li><li>Use and accurately attribute one detail from each source.</li><li>Compare a benefit and a limitation.</li><li>Give a conditional recommendation.</li><li>Propose a feasible next step.</li><li>Organize connected paragraphs rather than copying.</li></ul><p class="badge">Manual /8 · no automatic grade</p></section><h2 class="section-title" id="speaking">Speaking · 10 minutes</h2><section class="box" id="S1"><p class="eyebrow">speaking · S1</p><h2>Negotiate a bilingual activity</h2><p>Respond to four fixed prompts about a bilingual school activity. Each audio file already contains two plays; play it once, prepare 15 seconds and respond up to 30 seconds. Explain needs, compare choices, respond to an objection and confirm a conditional next step. All four responses form ONE /8 task; prompts are not adaptive.</p><p>You are planning a bilingual story-sharing activity with a classmate. All personal details can be invented.</p><ul class="checklist"><li>State a position linked to the partner’s needs.</li><li>Compare two choices with reasons.</li><li>Respond to a new restriction and revise a plan.</li><li>Explain a compromise and confirm the next step.</li></ul><h3>S1-1</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/s1-1.mp3"></audio><h3>S1-2</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/s1-2.mp3"></audio><h3>S1-3</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/s1-3.mp3"></audio><h3>S1-4</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/s1-4.mp3"></audio><p class="note">Each file already plays the prompt twice. Play it once; then prepare for 15 seconds and respond for up to 30 seconds. Four responses are one /8 task.</p><p class="badge">Manual /8 · no automatic grade</p></section><section class="box" id="S2"><p class="eyebrow">speaking · S2</p><h2>Choose a community information service</h2><p>Recommend a plan to the community center. Compare BOTH options, use at least two card details covering both, explain one trade-off and the conditions for your recommendation, and give a feasible next step. Either plan may earn full credit. Prepare 60 seconds; speak up to 120 seconds.</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">社区需求：本周六向四十位新访客介绍活动，部分访客不熟悉中文，也有人不用手机；预算一百元。<br>甲，咨询桌：两位双语志愿者轮流接待，免费；每次一对一，需要排队；下午两点后一位志愿者离开。<br>乙，自助信息卡：印刷八十元，有两种文字，可多人同时阅读；临时变动需要重新印；没有人专门回答追问。<br>中心可提前登记常见问题，但本次不能增加工作人员。</p></div><ul class="checklist"><li>Compare both plans accurately.</li><li>Use at least two details covering both options.</li><li>Explain one trade-off and a condition.</li><li>Give an audience-appropriate next step.</li></ul><p class="badge">Manual /8 · no automatic grade</p></section></main></body></html>